<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Maradi</h1><p class="st-meta">1819 CE – 1899 CE (approx.) · capital Maradi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The refuge state of the exiled Hausa rulers of Katsina in southern Niger, which spent the 19th century raiding the Fulani emirates to the south.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> jihadists took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/katsina-kingdom">Katsina</a> in 1807, its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> ruling family fled north. After years of wandering they settled at Maradi around 1819, where local Katsinawa rose against their Fulani governors. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dan-kassawa">Dan Kassawa</a> the exiles founded a new state that claimed to continue the Katsina Kingdom and refused to recognise the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Maradi kept the titles and court of old <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/katsina-kingdom">Katsina</a>. Most of its people practised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, but the state allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gobir">Gobir</a>, later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-tsibiri">Sultanate of Tsibiri</a>, and with non-Muslim groups against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a>. Its army raided the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/katsina-emirate">Katsina Emirate</a> and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> almost every year, and the frontier between the two Katsinas was a zone of constant warfare.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1899 French forces reached the area, and Maradi was absorbed into the territory that became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-niger">Colony of Niger</a>. The town grew into a major commercial centre for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groundnut">groundnuts</a>, and its sultan remains a traditional ruler.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate